#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:42
msgid "checks that each named policy is in this ValueSet;"
msgstr "vérifie que chaque politique nommée figure dans ce ValueSet ;"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:44
msgid "decides as the <a0>GDHCN Trust Network: Personal Health Wallet</a0> process I describes."
msgstr "décide comme le décrit le processus I de <a0>GDHCN Trust Network: Personal Health Wallet</a0>."

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:7
msgid "Explicit and implied consent"
msgstr "Consentement explicite et consentement implicite"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:46
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Naming a policy only narrows the consents that apply, and it never overrides a prohibition. A credential with no {code0} is decided on all the pilgrim's applicable consents."
msgstr "Nommer une politique ne fait que restreindre les consentements applicables, et ne prévaut jamais sur une interdiction. Une attestation sans {code0} est évaluée au regard de l'ensemble des consentements applicables du pèlerin."

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:16
msgid "Naming the consent a VHL Receiver acts under"
msgstr "Nommer le consentement en vertu duquel agit un VHL Receiver"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:3
msgid "Terms of use"
msgstr "Conditions d'utilisation"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:5
msgid "The <a0>IPS.HAJJ.CONSENT ValueSet</a0> is this Trust Domain's terms of use: the policies a participant may say it acts under. It is recorded on the <a1>IPS-PILGRIMAGE Trust Domain</a1> in the GDHCN Trust IG. The GDHCN Administrative and Operational Framework 1.2 has no annex for this Trust Domain yet, so that record is drafted from this IG."
msgstr "Le <a0>ValueSet IPS.HAJJ.CONSENT</a0> constitue les conditions d'utilisation de ce domaine de confiance : les politiques en vertu desquelles un participant peut déclarer agir. Il est consigné dans le <a1>domaine de confiance IPS-PILGRIMAGE</a1> du GDHCN Trust IG. Le cadre administratif et opérationnel 1.2 du GDHCN ne comporte pas encore d'annexe pour ce domaine de confiance ; cette consignation est donc rédigée à partir de cet IG."

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:40
msgid "The VHL Sharer then:"
msgstr "Le VHL Sharer ensuite :"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:9
msgid "This guide follows the consent model of the <a0>GDHCN Trust Network: Personal Health Wallet</a0> guide, which is built on IHE Privacy Consent on FHIR (PCF) 1.1.0:"
msgstr "Ce guide suit le modèle de consentement du guide <a0>GDHCN Trust Network: Personal Health Wallet</a0>, qui repose sur IHE Privacy Consent on FHIR (PCF) 1.1.0 :"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:18
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Under the Verifiable Credential Option of IHE ITI VHL (ITI-YY5), a VHL Receiver retrieves the manifest with a credential it issues itself. It can name the consent policy it acts under in that credential's W3C VC 2.0 {code0}, with one <a0>Trust Domain policy</a0> entry per policy:"
msgstr "Dans le cadre de l'option Verifiable Credential d'IHE ITI VHL (ITI-YY5), un VHL Receiver récupère le manifeste avec une attestation qu'il émet lui-même. Il peut nommer la politique de consentement en vertu de laquelle il agit dans le {code0} W3C VC 2.0 de cette attestation, avec une entrée <a0>Trust Domain policy</a0> par politique :"

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:14
msgid "Consent directives travel with the document. The pilgrim's IPS (<a0>HajjIPS</a0>) carries the pilgrimage consents it is shared under, as consent entries, and lists them in its Advance Directives section. The Personal Health Wallet guide's process M (\"Add Consent Directives to a Shared or Issued Document\") describes the steps. The copy in the IPS is evidence for the receiver. The origin HIE enforces the copy in its own Consent Registry, because a signed IPS cannot show a later withdrawal."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:11
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Explicit consent. The pilgrim agrees by their own act: on their wallet, or to the counsellor, who records it. Each <a0>pilgrimage consent</a0> is an explicit consent, an opt-in: its {code0} includes the HL7 v3 ActConsentDirective code {code1}. It names its {code2} code and the code system version in {code3}, and its {code4} is the evidence: the consent text the pilgrim was shown, with their recorded act. The Personal Health Wallet guide's process L (\"Record Explicit Consent\") describes the steps. Both the verbal consent and the consent on the wallet in this guide's business processes are explicit consents."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:12
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Implied consent. The pilgrim does nothing, and the Trust Domain's default policy applies (HL7 ActConsentDirective {code0}). This Trust Domain is opt-in: its default is the IHE PCF implicit policy {code1}. With no pilgrimage consent, the IPS is not shared."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:43
#, python-brace-format
msgid "matches it against the {code0} of the pilgrim's pilgrimage consents (system and code);"
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/trust_domain_policy.md:1
#, python-brace-format
msgid "This Trust Domain enables data exchange mediated by the pilgrim, on the basis of the pilgrim's consent. The consents are recorded in the <a0>IPS.HAJJ.CONSENT CodeSystem</a0>, and each <a1>pilgrimage consent</a1> in a pilgrim's IPS names one of them in {code0}."
msgstr ""

#~ msgid "Consent directives travel with the document. The pilgrim's IPS (<a0>HajjIPS</a0>) carries the Hajj consents it is shared under, as consent entries, and lists them in its Advance Directives section. The Personal Health Wallet guide's process M (\"Add Consent Directives to a Shared or Issued Document\") describes the steps. The copy in the IPS is evidence for the receiver. The origin HIE enforces the copy in its own Consent Registry, because a signed IPS cannot show a later withdrawal."
#~ msgstr "Les directives de consentement accompagnent le document. L’IPS du pèlerin (<a0>HajjIPS</a0>) porte les consentements Hajj sous lesquels il est partagé, sous forme d’entrées de consentement, et les énumère dans sa section Directives anticipées (Advance Directives). Le processus M du guide Personal Health Wallet (« Add Consent Directives to a Shared or Issued Document ») en décrit les étapes. La copie contenue dans l’IPS sert de preuve au destinataire. La HIE d’origine applique la copie conservée dans son propre Consent Registry, car un IPS signé ne peut pas faire apparaître un retrait ultérieur."

#~ #, python-brace-format
#~ msgid "Explicit consent. The pilgrim agrees by their own act: on their wallet, or to the counsellor, who records it. Each <a0>Hajj consent</a0> is an explicit consent, an opt-in: its {code0} includes the HL7 v3 ActConsentDirective code {code1}. It names its {code2} code and the code system version in {code3}, and its {code4} is the evidence: the consent text the pilgrim was shown, with their recorded act. The Personal Health Wallet guide's process L (\"Record Explicit Consent\") describes the steps. Both the verbal consent and the consent on the wallet in this guide's business processes are explicit consents."
#~ msgstr "Consentement explicite. Le pèlerin donne son accord par un acte qui lui est propre : dans son portefeuille, ou auprès du conseiller, qui l’enregistre. Chaque <a0>consentement Hajj</a0> est un consentement explicite, une adhésion volontaire (opt-in) : son {code0} comprend le code {code1} de HL7 v3 ActConsentDirective. Il indique son code {code2} et la version du système de codes dans {code3}, et son {code4} en constitue la preuve : le texte de consentement présenté au pèlerin, accompagné de l’acte consigné. Le processus L du guide Personal Health Wallet (« Record Explicit Consent ») en décrit les étapes. Le consentement verbal et le consentement dans le portefeuille décrits dans les processus métier de ce guide sont tous deux des consentements explicites."

#~ #, python-brace-format
#~ msgid "Implied consent. The pilgrim does nothing, and the Trust Domain's default policy applies (HL7 ActConsentDirective {code0}). This Trust Domain is opt-in: its default is the IHE PCF implicit policy {code1}. With no Hajj consent, the IPS is not shared."
#~ msgstr "Consentement implicite. Le pèlerin ne fait rien, et la politique par défaut du Domaine de confiance s’applique (HL7 ActConsentDirective {code0}). Ce Domaine de confiance fonctionne par adhésion volontaire (opt-in) : sa valeur par défaut est la politique implicite IHE PCF {code1}. Sans consentement Hajj, l’IPS n’est pas partagé."

